# Intentionally contains no settings — only this warning.
#
# Dependency lifecycle scripts are blocked by default in pnpm 10, and
# `pnpm.onlyBuiltDependencies` in package.json is the allowlist, with re2 as its sole
# entry. That combination is what lets re2's native binding compile while everything
# else stays blocked.
#
# Do NOT add `ignore-scripts=true` here. It is a blanket setting that overrides the
# allowlist, so re2 never compiles — `require('re2')` then fails with MODULE_NOT_FOUND,
# SafeMatcher silently falls back to the backtracking JS engine, and the linear-time
# guarantee this tool advertises is gone. CI ran in exactly that state until 2026-08-18.
# The `--require-re2` gate and the CI engine assertion exist to catch this.
#
# Be careful adding any resolution-affecting setting here (auto-install-peers and
# friends): pnpm records those in the lockfile, so a mismatch fails
# `install --frozen-lockfile` outright with ERR_PNPM_LOCKFILE_CONFIG_MISMATCH.
